__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/frontend/static/admin/
**/frontend/static/**/*.css
**/frontend/static/**/*.css.map
**/frontend/static/*/js/
src/urbanlens/frontend/static/dashboard/images/
src/urbanlens/frontend/static/icons/unused/
src/urbanlens/media/
docs/screenshots/
.codeql/
.sqlmap/
# written into this checkout by the `infrastructure` repo's opslib
.ops-runs/

# Libraries (npm, etc)
node_modules
package-lock.json
.venv/
.venv_windows/

# Temporary files
*.out
*.tmp
*.swp
.*cache
sample_data/*.jpg
src/urbanlens/logs/*

# VSCode stuff per user (keep shared workspace config)
# `settings.json` is deliberately NOT un-ignored: it carries per-developer
# editor state. Its negation existed here for a long time but was overridden by
# a later literal `.vscode/settings.json` (last matching pattern wins), so the
# file has never been tracked in this repo's history. Removing the duplicate
# without removing the negation turned a dormant line into a force-include that
# even `.vscode/*` could not catch, so `git add -A` would have staged it.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.favorites.json
.coverage
CLAUDE.local.md
# Only the per-machine file. `settings.json` registers the hooks that protect
# CLAUDE.md and auto-format Python on write, and `.claude/agents/` holds the
# docs-finder/docs-writer definitions - CLAUDE.md promises all of that, so it
# has to be in the tree rather than on one laptop.
.claude/settings.local.json
.cursor/
docs/notes/ai/
docs/notes/geocoding-analysis/

# Secrets, authentication, etc
.env
# Provider API keys, read only by the ai-inference container. Committing this
# would defeat the split it exists for - see .env.ai-sample.
.env.ai
bin/conf/
bin/settings.py
.pgpass

# Database files
*.sqlite3-journal
*db.sqlite3
pgsql
sample_data/Google Takeout.csv

# mutmut copies the tree here to mutate it.
mutants/

docs/audits/codeql-findings.md

# Agent scratch files have landed at the repo root untracked more than once.
/_tmp*
/*.tmp.js

# Sphinx output, and the API tree autoapi generates from src/ on each build.
# Both are products of `bun run docs`; neither is edited by hand.
docs/_build/
docs/api/
